---
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
import InlineCommand from "../../components/InlineCommand.tsx";
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro";
import PromptExamples from "../../components/PromptExamples.tsx"; // New import
import TerminalBlock from "../../components/TerminalBlock";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";

const validationPrompts = [
	{
		id: "full-review",
		title: "Full Review",
		description: "Have the AI review the entire feature at once based off the acceptance criteria in the habit tracker task breakdown.",
		command:
			"Review the code for the habit tracker I've just implemented against the acceptance criteria in @docs/tasks/habit-tracker.md. For each criterion, tell me if it's met, partially met, or not met, and explain why. Highlight any areas where the implementation deviates or introduces potential issues based on the requirements.",
	},
	{
		id: "specific-task",
		title: "Specific Task",
		description: "If you find doing a full review of the feature at the end is too overwhelming, break it down and validate each task individually.",
		command: "Review the code for Task 3 of the @docs/task/habit-tracker.md. Ensure it accurately reflects the acceptance criterion for that task.",
	},
	{
		id: "test-plan",
		title: "Test Plan Generation",
		description: "If you would like to do some manual tests before proceeding, you can have the AI generate a test plan.",
		command:
			"Generate a manual testing plan for the Habit Tracker feature based on the acceptance criteria in @docs/tasks/habit-tracker.md. Include step-by-step instructions and expected results for each scenario.",
	},
];

const typeLintPrompts = [
	{
		id: "check-type-errors",
		title: "Check Type Errors",
		description: "Ask the AI to run the TypeScript compiler and interpret the errors, suggesting fixes.",
		command: "Run the TypeScript compiler with `pnpm typecheck`. If there are any type errors in the files I've changed, explain them and suggest a fix.",
	},
	{
		id: "run-linter",
		title: "Run Linter",
		description: "Ask the AI to run the linter, interpret its output, and apply fixes according to project standards.",
		command: "Run the linter over the files I've modified with `pnpm lint`. If it finds any issues, fix them according to our project's coding standards.",
	},
];
---

<MainLayout title="Validation Steps - AI Training Guide">
  <PageShell chapterId="practical-exercise" subChapterId="validation-steps">
    <div class="prose space-y-6">
      <p>
        You've moved from requirements to tasks and then to implementation. Now it's time to ensure your work
        is correct, robust, and meets all expectations. In this chapter, you'll learn how to leverage AI to
        validate your completed features, catching issues earlier and ensuring higher quality code.
      </p>

      <!-- ─── Step 1 ─── -->
      <div class="relative border-l-4 border-teal-400 pl-6 py-2 my-10">
        <div class="absolute -left-4 top-2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-teal-500 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">1</div>
        <h3 class="mt-0 mb-2">Validate Against Task Breakdown</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4 mt-4">
          The first step in validating your work is to check it against the acceptance criteria defined in your
          task breakdown. AI can be a powerful assistant in this process, and when you give it clear guidelines, 
          it will take on the role of your QA engineer.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700 mb-2 font-medium">
          Instruct the AI to review your implementation against the specific task file. For the habit tracker feature,
          you'll reference <InlineCommand command="@docs/tasks/habit-tracker.md" client:visible />.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700 mb-2 font-medium">
            Below we'll provide some sample prompts for various testing scenarios:
        </p>

        <PromptExamples prompts={validationPrompts} client:visible />

        <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-2">
          This approach helps you quickly identify whether your code fulfills the stated requirements, acting as an
          early warning system for potential bugs or misunderstandings.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ─── Step 2 ─── -->
      <div class="relative border-l-4 border-teal-400 pl-6 py-2 my-10">
        <div class="absolute -left-4 top-2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-teal-500 text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">2</div>
        <h3 class="mt-0 mb-2">Run Type & Lint Checks with AI</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4">
          Prior to pushing your changes, you should also be running automated checks like type validation and linting. AI can not only help you
          run these checks but also interpret their output and even suggest fixes.
        </p>

        <PromptExamples prompts={typeLintPrompts} client:visible />

        <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-2">
          By integrating AI into your type and linting workflow, you can maintain a cleaner codebase with fewer manual
          interventions, allowing you to focus on more complex logic.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ─── Forward-Looking Guidance ─── -->
      <div class="border-t border-stone-200">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-800 mb-4">Forward-Looking Guidance</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4">
          Validation is the final critical step in the iterative development cycle. The full loop now looks like:{" "}
          <strong>Requirements → Tasks → Implementation → Validation</strong>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4">
            AI assists you at every single stage. Critically, the developer remains firmly in control throughout this 
            entire process. You guide the AI, review its output, and make the ultimate decisions since, ultimately, 
            the code is yours. This continuous feedback loop leads to faster development cycles and higher quality outcomes. 
        </p>
        <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mb-4">
          <strong>Apply these validation techniques to all future features you develop in the following lessons.</strong> Make it a habit to integrate AI into
          your testing and verification workflow. The more consistently you use these steps, the more reliable and
          efficient your development process will become.
        </p>
        <p class="text-stone-800 font-medium">
          By making validation a core part of your AI-assisted workflow, you're not just building features faster, you're
          building them better.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </PageShell>
</MainLayout>
